[h1]Save Item Spots[/h1]

Save 3D Placement for items on tiles, then restore any item to that exact position and rotation later. Share saved positions with other players and factions.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*] Save the position and rotation of any placed world item as a named preset
[*] Restore any item from your inventory to a saved position
[*] Multiple presets per tile (configurable, default 5)
[*] Multiplayer compatible — position data syncs via tile modData
[*] Share positions with specific players or entire factions (UNTESTED, MIGHT NOT WORK YET)
[/list]

[h2]How to Use[/h2]

[h3]Save a Position[/h3]
[olist]
[*] Place an item on the ground/surface where you want it
[*] Adjust its position with the vanilla 3D Placement tool until it looks right
[*] Right-click the item on the ground inventory panel → [b]Save Position[/b]
[*] Enter a name for the preset
[/olist]

[h3]Restore an Item[/h3]
[b]From inventory:[/b] Right-click an item → [b]Place at Saved Position[/b] → select a preset. Your character walks to the tile and places the item at the saved offsets and rotation.

[b]From tile:[/b] Right-click a tile with saved presets → [b]Place Saved Item[/b] → select a preset → choose an item from your inventory.

[h3]Sharing (Untested — Use at Your Own Risk)[/h3]
[i]Note: Sharing functionality is included but has not been tested. It may not work correctly yet. Please report any issues on the Workshop page or GitHub.[/i]
[list]
[*] Positions are private by default (only the creator can see them)
[*] Right-click a tile → open "Item Spots" panel → share presets with players or your faction
[*] Shared players/faction members see the presets in their context menus
[*] Recipients can [b]Forget[/b] a shared position to hide it from their view
[/list]

[h2]Configuration[/h2]
[table]
[tr][th]Option[/th][th]Default[/th][th]Description[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]Max Presets Per Tile[/td][td]5[/td][td]Maximum number of saved positions per tile (1-20)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Show Coordinates in Preset Names[/td][td]true[/td][td]Show tile coordinates next to preset names in context menus[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Filter Equipped Items[/td][td]true[/td][td]Hide equipped items from the "Place Saved Item" list[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[h2]Scope & Limitations[/h2]
[list]
[*] Works with [b]world inventory items[/b] (items on the ground/surfaces) only
[*] Does [b]NOT[/b] work with moveables/furniture (shelves, tables, fridges, etc.)
[*] Items of different sizes may clip slightly when placed at a position saved by a different-sized item
[*] You cannot create two presets with the same name on the same tile.
[/list]

[h2]Known Issues[/h2]
[list]
[*] Tile weight limit might not enforced properly. More testing needed.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*] Project Zomboid Build 42.20+
[*] Multiplayer dedicated servers and singleplayer
[*] No dependencies
[*] Does not conflict with other mods
[/list]

